{"name":"Ginger Lemon Tea","hex":"#ffffaa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"ginger","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The pungent aromatic rhizome of a tropical Asian herb, Zingiber officinale, used as a spice and as a stimulant and acarminative.","The plant that produces this rhizome."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a reddish-brown color.","Having hair or fur of this color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ginger"},{"term":"lemon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish citrus fruit.","A semitropical evergreen tree, Citrus limon, that bears such fruits."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavour/flavor and/or scent of lemons.","Of the pale yellow colour/color of lemons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon"},{"term":"tea","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Temiar."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The tea plant (Camellia sinensis);  a variety of this plant.","The dried leaves or buds of the tea plant;  a variety of such leaves."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tea culture","blocks":[{"text":"Tea culture is the culture around the preparation and drinking of tea and the private and social settings in which this occurs."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Japanese_tea_ceremony_20100502_Japan_Matsuri_02.jpg/330px-Japanese_tea_ceremony_20100502_Japan_Matsuri_02.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea_culture","wikidata":"Q4348225"},{"title":"Ginger","blocks":[{"text":"Ginger is a flowering plant whose rhizome, ginger root or ginger, is widely used as a spice and a folk medicine. It is an herbaceous perennial that grows annual pseudostems about one meter tall, bearing narrow leaf blades. The inflorescences bear flowers having pale yellow petals with purple edges, and arise directly from the rhizome on separate shoots."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Koeh-146-no_text.jpg/330px-Koeh-146-no_text.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginger","wikidata":"Q35625"},{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Kustodiev_Merchants_Wife.jpg/500px-Kustodiev_Merchants_Wife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Kustodiev_Merchants_Wife.jpg/500px-Kustodiev_Merchants_Wife.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbna